8. Merchant Onboarding and Marketplace Selection Fixes

Fix the current onboarding behavior.

8.1 Marketplace selection must be optional and dynamic

The current onboarding incorrectly forces Amazon to remain selected or forces the merchant to select another option before removing it.

This is wrong.

Requirements:

- No marketplace is selected by default.
- Amazon must not be mandatory.
- Noon must not be mandatory.
- Every marketplace selection must be independently selectable and deselectable.
- The merchant can deselect a marketplace directly without selecting another one.
- The merchant can continue without selecting any marketplace.
- Do not automatically select Amazon as the first marketplace.
- Do not force the merchant to choose from a fixed list.

The marketplace selection interface must support multiple selections naturally.

8.2 Website name input

When the merchant selects "My Own Store / Website", immediately display a text field:

"Enter your website or store name"

Allow the merchant to enter a name or domain.

Do not treat all websites as one generic marketplace.

Store the website name as a separate merchant channel with its own stable internal identifier.

8.3 Save onboarding selections once

The current application asks newly registered merchants to select Amazon and Noon again after they have already completed onboarding.

Fix this.

Rules:

- Save the merchant's initial selections.
- Load those saved selections on subsequent visits.
- Do not repeat onboarding after successful completion.
- Do not automatically add Amazon or Noon.
- Allow marketplace management later through Settings.
- Existing merchant selections must remain unchanged after this update.
- If a merchant has no marketplace selected, do not force a selection later.

The onboarding process must never overwrite existing merchant configuration without confirmation.

