9. Redesign the Learning and Tutorial Experience

The current tutorials feel forced, visually weak, and inconsistent.

Redesign the entire learning experience.

9.1 Tutorial interface

Requirements:

- Large, readable instruction panel.
- Clear typography.
- Comfortable spacing.
- Simple explanations.
- Interactive 3D guide character.
- Smooth, subtle transitions.
- A clear visual highlight around the exact element being explained.
- Dim unrelated elements slightly without making the page difficult to see.

The tutorial must point to the actual interface element being explained.

The highlight should be visible around each relevant field, button, card, menu, and control—not only on the dashboard.

9.2 Character interaction

Use the existing 3D character concept:

- Professional male character.
- Business suit.
- Proportional body.
- Featureless face without eyes, nose, or mouth.
- Real 3D appearance, not a flat illustration.

The character should have subtle idle and guidance animations where technically supported.

Do not substitute a static image and claim that a fully interactive 3D character has been implemented.

If a proper 3D asset or rendering capability is missing, explain the limitation and implement the best supported foundation without breaking the rest of the application.

9.3 Tutorial controls

Provide:

- Next.
- Back.
- I Understand.
- Skip Tutorial.
- Restart Tutorial.

The merchant must remain in control.

Do not force the same tutorial to appear repeatedly.

Save tutorial progress per merchant.

Allow tutorials to be reopened from the Learning Center.

